WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:14.590
Unit twenty: Have / Has (possession). Today you will say what people own with have and has.

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.507
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.456
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.317 --> 00:00:23.144
Have.

7
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.370
Have means to own or to possess.

8
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:28.286
I have a bike.

9
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:31.269
Your turn. Say: Have.

10
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:34.995
Have.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.635
Has.

12
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.033
Has means the form of have for he, she and it.

13
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.804
She has a pet.

14
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.790
Your turn. Say: Has.

15
00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:48.460
Has.

16
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:49.974
Brother.

17
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.621
Brother means a boy or man with the same parents.

18
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:55.438
I have one brother.

19
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.586
Your turn. Say: Brother.

20
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:02.249
Brother.

21
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:03.892
Sister.

22
00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:07.951
Sister means a girl or woman with the same parents.

23
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.865
She has a sister.

24
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.789
Your turn. Say: Sister.

25
00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:16.495
Sister.

26
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:17.914
Pet.

27
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:21.183
Pet means an animal that lives with you.

28
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:23.051
My pet is a cat.

29
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.151
Your turn. Say: Pet.

30
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:29.792
Pet.

31
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.238
Bike.

32
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.993
Bike means a two-wheeled vehicle you ride.

33
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:37.258
I ride my bike to school.

34
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.386
Your turn. Say: Bike.

35
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:44.060
Bike.

36
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:45.864
Don't have.

37
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.908
Don't have means not to own something.

38
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:50.820
I don't have a car.

39
00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:53.628
Your turn. Say: Don't have.

40
00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.514
Don't have.

41
00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.344
Doesn't have.

42
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.824
Doesn't have means he, she or it does not own something.

43
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.929
He doesn't have a pet.

44
00:02:06.517 --> 00:02:09.715
Your turn. Say: Doesn't have.

45
00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:13.742
Doesn't have.

46
00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:18.335
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:22.300
Visal, what do you have at home? Do you have a pet?

48
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:34.596
I have a cat. We use have with I, you, we and they: I have a cat. They have a house. We use has with he, she and it: She has a bike.

49
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:37.184
How do we make negatives?

50
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:47.556
Use don't have or doesn't have: I don't have a car. He doesn't have a brother. After doesn't, the verb is have, not has.

51
00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.930
And questions?

52
00:02:51.017 --> 00:03:02.570
Do you have a brother? Does she have a pet? We answer: Yes, I do. No, she doesn't. Have and has are often used for family and things we own.

53
00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:05.268
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:08.488
Grammar focus: Have and has.

55
00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.126
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:11.945
I have a brother.

57
00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.257
She has a pet cat.

58
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.615
He doesn't have a bike.

59
00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:24.550
Use have with I, you, we and they, and has with he, she and it. In questions and negatives with do or does, use have.

60
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:28.168
Be careful! Don't say: She have a pet.

61
00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.796
Say: She has a pet.

62
00:03:32.096 --> 00:03:33.945
Use has with he, she and it.

63
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:37.420
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:39.873
My Family and Things.

65
00:03:40.173 --> 00:03:42.277
I have one brother and two sisters.

66
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:46.160
My brother has a bike, but my sister doesn't have a bike.

67
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.944
We have a pet cat, and it has a long tail.

68
00:03:50.933 --> 00:03:52.329
Do you have a pet at home?

69
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.331
Some people don't have pets, but they love animals.

70
00:03:57.433 --> 00:04:01.447
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:03.749
She blank a new bike.

72
00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:07.238
A, have. B, has. C, haves.

73
00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.649
The answer is B: has.

74
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:15.365
They blank two cats.

75
00:04:15.665 --> 00:04:18.749
A, has. B, have. C, having.

76
00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.149
The answer is B: have.

77
00:04:25.283 --> 00:04:26.853
He doesn't blank a car.

78
00:04:27.153 --> 00:04:30.145
A, has. B, have. C, had.

79
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.758
The answer is B: have.

80
00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:38.603
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:38.903 --> 00:04:43.079
A, I has a pen.. B, I have a pen.. C, I haves a pen..

82
00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:48.877
The answer is B: I have a pen..

83
00:04:50.017 --> 00:04:52.225
According to the reading, who has a bike?

84
00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:56.004
A, my brother. B, my sister. C, my cat.

85
00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.822
The answer is A: my brother.

86
00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:06.138
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:06.983 --> 00:05:08.902
What do you have in your school bag?

88
00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.171
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:19.471 --> 00:05:33.901
I have a notebook, two pens and a water bottle in my school bag. I don't have a laptop. My friend has a ruler and a small calculator. I use have with I and has with he or she.

90
00:05:34.201 --> 00:05:36.049
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:41.088
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and have and has.

92
00:05:41.388 --> 00:05:45.573
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

93
00:05:45.873 --> 00:05:48.758
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:05:49.058 --> 00:05:51.397
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

